 and its erlang-* dependency chain (odbc, snmp, os-mon, ssh, tools, etc.) finished installing successfully on node3 without an apt kill/retry.\"},{\"source\":\"node2 command sequence 01:38–01:46 (four ~60-120s sleep/poll commands)\",\"finding\":\"apt-get install -y -qq rabbitmq-server on node2 was still running (root apt-get + apt-get + _apt http method processes alive) after roughly 8+ minutes with no dpkg output for rabbitmq-server, i.e. it appeared stalled or extremely slow.\"},{\"source\":\"node2, 01:46:58\",\"finding\":\"Executor killed the stuck apt-get with 'pkill -9 apt-get' and 'pkill -9 -f /usr/lib/apt/methods', then ran dpkg --configure -a, and started a second install (install2.log).\"},{\"source\":\"node2 install2.log polling 01:48–01:55 (three more sleep/poll commands)\",\"finding\":\"The retried install also ran for roughly 8+ minutes with apt-get and the _apt http method process still alive; dpkg -l did not yet show rabbitmq-server.\"},{\"source\":\"node2 and node3, 01:58:24\",\"finding\":\"ss -tlnp on both node2 and node3 shows RabbitMQ ports (4369, 5672, 25672) listening — RabbitMQ eventually came up on both nodes.\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 01:58:28\",\"finding\":\"rabbitmqadmin was fetched from the local management plugin and both Python 2.7.12 and 3.5.2 were present.\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 01:58:32\",\"finding\":\"rabbitmqadmin declare queue against vhost 'payments' as user app_payments returned 'Access refused: /api/queues/payments/orders' (HTTP 403-equivalent).\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 01:58:37–02:00:52\",\"finding\":\"pika was not installed; python3-pip was missing; an attempt to apt-get install python3-pip timed out at the 120s MCP proxy read-timeout window (the underlying apt-get process was still running and later completed on its own).\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 02:03:20\",\"finding\":\"pip3 install of the latest pika (1.4.4) succeeded, but importing it raised 'SyntaxError: invalid syntax' on the line using a Python 3.6+ variable-annotation (`self._blocked_connection_timeout: Optional[float] = None`) — incompatible with the system Python 3.5.2 on Ubuntu 16.04.\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 02:03:46\",\"finding\":\"Downgrading to pika==1.1.0 installed cleanly and imported successfully (version 1.1.0 confirmed).\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 02:04:28\",\"finding\":\"A pika-based publish script ran successfully, printing 'publish_confirmed None' — publish succeeded but the confirm result value was None rather than an explicit True, which is unusual for a delivery-confirm publish and unverified/unexplained in the available evidence.\"},{\"source\":\"node1, 02:04:32\",\"finding\":\"rabbitmqctl list_queues on vhost payments showed queue 'orders' with durable=true and slave_pids/synchronised_slave_pids listing rabbit@node3 and rabbit@node2 — i.e., the durable queue was mirrored to two nodes at that point.\"},{\"source\":\"audit summary metadata\",\"finding\":\"Only 31 of 150 total command records were included in this redacted trace (up to 20 recent failures + 12 recent successes); 119 records, including whatever vhost/user/permission setup happened earlier, were omitted. No records show the actual `payments` vhost creation, app_payments user creation, or `set_permissions` calls.\"},{\"source\":\"attempt metadata\",\"finding\":\"Attempt terminated by executor_timed_out after 2100 seconds; no record in the provided trace shows a node being stopped/killed nor a consume-after-node-loss check being performed.\"}],\"likely_causes\":[{\"cause\":\"Package installation for rabbitmq-server (and its large erlang-* dependency set) via apt-get on this Ubuntu 16.04 image was very slow and/or intermittently stalled, consuming on the order of 15-20+ minutes of wall-clock time across node2 alone (initial hang + kill + retry), which is a large fraction of the 2100s budget.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"cause\":\"The default/latest pika client version is incompatible with the system Python 3.5 interpreter shipped on this Ubuntu 16.04 image, causing an import-time SyntaxError; this was only discovered after installing python3-pip and pika from scratch, adding further delay.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"cause\":\"'Access refused' from rabbitmqadmin/management API for the app_payments user on the payments vhost indicates the account was missing vhost permissions (or the vhost/user/permission setup had a mistake) at the time management-API access was attempted; not enough evidence in the trace to confirm the exact misconfiguration since the setup commands are outside the redacted window.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"The combination of the above delays (apt stalls, python/pika version mismatch, pivoting from rabbitmqadmin to raw pika scripts) consumed most of the time budget, so the task likely ran out of time before it could kill a node and verify the durable queue was still consumable from the survivors — the required end-to-end resilience test was not observed to have run.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"}],\"next_attempt_guidance\":[\"Kick off `apt-get update` and `apt-get install -y rabbitmq-server` on all three nodes in parallel/background immediately at the start, and poll less frequently with longer intervals (or a single longer background job) rather than issuing repeated 60-120s sleep+poll commands that eat wall-clock time without acting; if a node's apt-get shows no progress for ~3-4 minutes, kill and retry once, not repeatedly.\",\"Pin pika to a version known to work with the system Python (3.5.x on Ubuntu 16.04) up front — use `pip3 install 'pika==1.1.0'` directly instead of installing the latest version first and discovering the incompatibility.\",\"Before relying on rabbitmqadmin/management HTTP API, explicitly create the `payments` vhost and grant the app account full permissions with `rabbitmqctl add_vhost payments` and `rabbitmqctl set_permissions -p payments <user> '.*' '.*' '.*'`, and confirm with `rabbitmqctl list_permissions -p payments` before attempting to declare queues via the API — this avoids the 'Access refused' detour.\",\"Consider skipping the management-API/rabbitmqadmin path entirely for validation and using rabbitmqctl + a pinned pika client from the st
