importing it raised 'SyntaxError: invalid syntax' on the line using a Python 3.6+ variable-annotation (`self._blocked_connection_timeout: Optional[float] = None`) — incompatible with the system Python 3.5.2 on Ubuntu 16.04."},{"source":"node1, 02:03:46","finding":"Downgrading to pika==1.1.0 installed cleanly and imported successfully (version 1.1.0 confirmed)."},{"source":"node1, 02:04:28","finding":"A pika-based publish script ran successfully, printing 'publish_confirmed None' — publish succeeded but the confirm result value was None rather than an explicit True, which is unusual for a delivery-confirm publish and unverified/unexplained in the available evidence."},{"source":"node1, 02:04:32","finding":"rabbitmqctl list_queues on vhost payments showed queue 'orders' with durable=true and slave_pids/synchronised_slave_pids listing rabbit@node3 and rabbit@node2 — i.e., the durable queue was mirrored to two nodes at that point."},{"source":"audit summary metadata","finding":"Only 31 of 150 total command records were included in this redacted trace (up to 20 recent failures + 12 recent successes); 119 records, including whatever vhost/user/permission setup happened earlier, were omitted. No records show the actual `payments` vhost creation, app_payments user creation, or `set_permissions` calls."},{"source":"attempt metadata","finding":"Attempt terminated by executor_timed_out after 2100 seconds; no record in the provided trace shows a node being stopped/killed nor a consume-after-node-loss check being performed."}],"likely_causes":[{"cause":"Package installation for rabbitmq-server (and its large erlang-* dependency set) via apt-get on this Ubuntu 16.04 image was very slow and/or intermittently stalled, consuming on the order of 15-20+ minutes of wall-clock time across node2 alone (initial hang + kill + retry), which is a large fraction of the 2100s budget.","confidence":"high"},{"cause":"The default/latest pika client version is incompatible with the system Python 3.5 interpreter shipped on this Ubuntu 16.04 image, causing an import-time SyntaxError; this was only discovered after installing python3-pip and pika from scratch, adding further delay.","confidence":"high"},{"cause":"'Access refused' from rabbitmqadmin/management API for the app_payments user on the payments vhost indicates the account was missing vhost permissions (or the vhost/user/permission setup had a mistake) at the time management-API access was attempted; not enough evidence in the trace to confirm the exact misconfiguration since the setup commands are outside the redacted window.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"The combination of the above delays (apt stalls, python/pika version mismatch, pivoting from rabbitmqadmin to raw pika scripts) consumed most of the time budget, so the task likely ran out of time before it could kill a node and verify the durable queue was still consumable from the survivors — the required end-to-end resilience test was not observed to have run.","confidence":"medium"}],"next_attempt_guidance":["Kick off `apt-get update` and `apt-get install -y rabbitmq-server` on all three nodes in parallel/background immediately at the start, and poll less frequently with longer intervals (or a single longer background job) rather than issuing repeated 60-120s sleep+poll commands that eat wall-clock time without acting; if a node's apt-get shows no progress for ~3-4 minutes, kill and retry once, not repeatedly.","Pin pika to a version known to work with the system Python (3.5.x on Ubuntu 16.04) up front — use `pip3 install 'pika==1.1.0'` directly instead of installing the latest version first and discovering the incompatibility.","Before relying on rabbitmqadmin/management HTTP API, explicitly create the `payments` vhost and grant the app account full permissions with `rabbitmqctl add_vhost payments` and `rabbitmqctl set_permissions -p payments <user> '.*' '.*' '.*'`, and confirm with `rabbitmqctl list_permissions -p payments` before attempting to declare queues via the API — this avoids the 'Access refused' detour.","Consider skipping the management-API/rabbitmqadmin path entirely for validation and using rabbitmqctl + a pinned pika client from the start, since that is what ultimately worked here.","Reserve explicit time in the run for the actual resilience test: after the queue is confirmed mirrored (durable=true with slave_pids on the other nodes), stop rabbitmq-server (or the whole node) on the master node, then verify the queue and message are still present and consumable from a surviving node before declaring success — this step was not evidenced as completed in the timed-out attempt.","Given apt/package installation was the single largest time sink observed, consider pre-warming or caching the rabbitmq-server package/dependencies if the image or environment allows it, or budget significantly more of the time allowance to installation before starting configuration steps."],"summary":"The attempt timed out after 2100s without evidence of completing the required resilience test. Observed facts: RabbitMQ installation via apt-get was slow and stalled on node2, requiring a kill and reinstall (each install phase took 8+ minutes); on node1, python3-pip was missing and had to be installed, then the latest pika (1.4.4) failed to import due to a Python 3.5 syntax incompatibility, requiring a downgrade to pika==1.1.0; an earlier attempt to use rabbitmqadmin against the payments vhost returned 'Access refused' for the app account, causing a pivot to raw pika scripts. By the last recorded action, a durable queue 'orders' had been created and mirrored to two nodes and a message had been published, but no evidence in the trace shows a node being killed or consumption from survivors being verified — likely because time ran out. The redacted trace omits 119 of 150 commands, including the vhost/user/permission setup, so the root cause of the 'Access refused' error cannot be confirmed from available evidence."},"ttft_ms":33181,"type":"result","duration_ms":63796,"uuid":"e523452e-5630-4794-a545-8c94ae15a8dc","ttft_stream_ms":2843,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":3544,"queued_turn_count":0}
